  "reasoning": [
    "compiler_identity binds the requested command, resolved argv, invocation path/realpath, driver SHA256, full version, target, cc1plus/as/ld paths and hashes, and relevant toolchain environment.",
    "build_key includes compiler identity, flags, ordered source units, builder SHA256 and source digest. GCC 13 and GCC 14 have distinct build keys, drivers, cc1plus and executable hashes.",
    "build_exporter validates sources and probes compiler identity before the skip branch. --no-build checks every request field, full ledger, native digest and actual executable hash, then rechecks source and compiler before returning. The render caller always invokes it.",
    "Fresh exporters compile all five generation translation units plus the exporter directly in a private temporary path. They do not consume shared Make objects. Success replaces the executable and marker only after compile and identity checks.",
    "The Interlaced renderer runs the returned private executable for layer checks and every native material capture, and seals HEAD, tree, inputs, index and source archive before/after rendering.",
    "qualify_interlaced invokes make -B with the requested CXX, forcing all six generation object dependencies and the test to rebuild. The original build log confirms all six GCC 13 compilations. The repaired CLASSIC parent is independently extracted and compiled in a temporary directory.",
    "The original comparator requires exact source boundaries, actual distinct GCC majors and driver/cache/executable identities, verifies all 26 parameters, and compares raw cells, PNG bytes, fingerprints and chunk receipts. Failure evidence is retained and the CLI returns nonzero."
  ],
